Exact security/RPA model retired from default production at K5582a10c5ec8.
The pre-removal hashes and caller/three-class audit are in the userspace
security-state-retirement-audit-20261014.json. legacy_ioctls.rs,
legacy_ral_dispatch.rs and legacy_pairing_worker.rs retain original bodies.

Only run_security_remediation.py includes this model. Its 7 tests are historical
state/semantic/failure regression, not current Runtime or hardware security.
It separately compiles unchanged net/sparklink/sle_crypto.rs wrappers and actual
sle_crypto_ffi.c CTR body against counted fault dependencies (5 C stages).
The kernel mechanism sources remain in net/sparklink for future authenticated
per-session security, but have no default object/module consumer. Do not restore
controller-global state or wire responders. Real key installation, standard
vectors, authentication, zeroization and VM peer security gates remain missing.
